{
  "moduleId": "m00348",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00348:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Some Examples of Sigmatropic Rearrangements"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "ce8c5b6d-32f4-4153-b6f9-fdec12d65639"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00348:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00348:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "5-methyl-1,3-cyclopentadiene reacts through 1,5-shift to form 1-methyl-1,3-cyclopentadiene. This undergoes 1,5-shift to form 2-methyl-1,3-cyclopentadiene"
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_30_08_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00348:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00348:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "5,5,5-trideuterio-(3Z)-1,3-pentadiene reacts with heat via [1,5] shift to give a pentadiene in which one D has migrated from C 5 to C 1."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_30_08_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00348:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00348:caption:fig-00003-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00348:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "Orbital representation of suprafacial 1,5-hydrogen shift. P orbitals on C 1 and C 5 are in-phase with each other. Hydrogen bonded to same-phase lobes on both carbons in transition state."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_30_08_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00348:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00348:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "An allylic aryl ether reacts to form o-allylphenol and an allylic vinylic ether reacts to form unsaturated ketone through Claisen rearrangement. 1,5-diene reacts to form isomeric 1,5-diene through Cope rearrangement."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_30_08_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00348:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00005",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00348:caption:fig-00005-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00348:alt:fig-00005-alt",
          "text": "Allyl phenyl ether undergoes Claisen rearrangement that reacts via a transition state to form an intermediate, 6-allyl-2,4-cyclohexadienone. This further reacts to form o-allylphenol."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_18_04_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00006",
      "segmentId": "m00348:para:para-00006"
    },
